          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Solution :",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Using the distance formula, we have"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.147,
            0.167,
            0.637,
            0.193
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_5_equation_3.jpg",
          "content": "AB = \\sqrt{\\left(6-3\\right)^{2}+\\left(4-1\\right)^{2}}=\\sqrt{9+9}=\\sqrt{18}=3\\sqrt{2}."
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.147,
            0.202,
            0.635,
            0.227
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_5_equation_4.jpg",
          "content": "\\mathrm{BC} = \\sqrt{\\left( 8 - 6 \\right)^{2} + \\left( 6 - 4 \\right)^{2}} = \\sqrt{4 + 4} = \\sqrt{8} = 2\\sqrt{2}"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.148,
            0.237,
            0.664,
            0.263
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_5_equation_5.jpg",
          "content": "AC  = \\sqrt{ \\left( 8 - 3 \\right)^{2} + \\left( 6 - 1 \\right)^{2} } = \\sqrt{ 25 + 25 } = \\sqrt{ 50 } = 5\\sqrt{ 2 }"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.275,
            0.901,
            0.321
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Since, "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "AB + BC = 3\\sqrt{2} + 2\\sqrt{2} = 5\\sqrt{2} = AC"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " ,  we can say that the points A, B and C are collinear. Therefore, they are seated in a line."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.333,
            0.901,
            0.373
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Example 4 :",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Find a relation between x and y such that the point (x , y) is equidistant from the points (7, 1) and (3, 5)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.378,
            0.789,
            0.397
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Solution :",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Let "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm { P } ( x , y )"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " be equidistant from the points A(7, 1) and B(3, 5)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.402,
            0.515,
            0.422
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We are given that "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm{AP} = \\mathrm{BP}. \\mathrm{So}, \\mathrm{AP}^2 = \\mathrm{BP}^2"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.098,
            0.429,
            0.139,
            0.447
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "i.e.,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.292,
            0.427,
            0.675,
            0.448
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_5_equation_11.jpg",
          "content": "(x - 7)^{2} + (y - 1)^{2} = (x - 3)^{2} + (y - 5)^{2}"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.098,
            0.454,
            0.139,
            0.472
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "i.e.,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.205,
            0.453,
            0.758,
            0.473
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_5_equation_13.jpg",
          "content": "x^{2}-14x+49+y^{2}-2y+1=x^{2}-6x+9+y^{2}-10y+25"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.098,
            0.479,
            0.14,
            0.497
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "i.e.,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.414,
            0.479,
            0.514,
            0.498
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_5_equation_15.jpg",
          "content": "x - y = 2"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.512,
            0.385,
            0.531
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "which is the required relation."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.544,
            0.518,
            0.681
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Remark :",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Note that the graph of the equation "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "x - y = 2"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is a line. From your earlier studies, you know that a point which is equidistant from A and B lies on the perpendicular bisector of AB. Therefore, the graph of "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "x - y = 2"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is the perpendicular bisector of AB (see Fig. 7.7)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.687,
            0.516,
            0.746
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Example 5 :",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Find a point on the y-axis which is equidistant from the points "
